# Data Handling Patterns

## Overview
All database operations flow through centralized query functions in `src/db/queries/`. Components and server actions never import `db` or `schema` directly — they consume query functions exclusively.

## Architecture

```
src/db/
├── index.ts          # Drizzle client (only imported by query files)
├── schema.ts         # Table & relation definitions (only imported by query files)
└── queries/
    ├── index.ts      # Re-exports everything from decks.ts & cards.ts
    ├── decks.ts      # Deck reads + writes
    └── cards.ts      # Card reads + writes (always verify deck ownership)
```

### Import Rules

| Layer | May import from `@/db/queries` | May import from `@/db` or `@/db/schema` |
|---|---|---|
| Server Components | Yes | **No** |
| Server Actions | Yes | **No** |
| `src/db/queries/*` | N/A | Yes |

```typescript
// ✅ Server Component or Server Action
import { getUserDecks } from "@/db/queries";

// ❌ NEVER in a component or action
import { db } from "@/db";
import { decksTable } from "@/db/schema";
```

## Query Function Conventions

Every function in `src/db/queries/` must:

1. Call `auth()` and reject if `!userId`.
2. Scope every query to the authenticated user (decks by `userId`, cards by verifying parent deck ownership).
3. Return data directly — no HTTP-style wrappers.

### Deck Queries (`src/db/queries/decks.ts`)

```typescript
import { auth } from "@clerk/nextjs/server";
import { db } from "@/db";
import { decksTable, cardsTable } from "@/db/schema";
import { eq, and, sql, desc } from "drizzle-orm";

// Read — list all decks for the current user (with card count)
export async function getUserDecks() {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) throw new Error("Unauthorized");

  return await db
    .select({
      id: decksTable.id,
      title: decksTable.title,
      description: decksTable.description,
      userId: decksTable.userId,
      createdAt: decksTable.createdAt,
      updatedAt: decksTable.updatedAt,
      cardCount: sql<number>`COUNT(${cardsTable.id})`.as("cardCount"),
    })
    .from(decksTable)
    .leftJoin(cardsTable, eq(decksTable.id, cardsTable.deckId))
    .where(eq(decksTable.userId, userId))
    .groupBy(decksTable.id)
    .orderBy(desc(decksTable.updatedAt));
}

// Read — single deck by ID (scoped to user)
export async function getDeckById(deckId: number) {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) throw new Error("Unauthorized");

  const deck = await db
    .select()
    .from(decksTable)
    .where(and(eq(decksTable.id, deckId), eq(decksTable.userId, userId)))
    .limit(1);

  return deck[0] || null;
}

// Write — create (enforces free-tier limit via canCreateDeck)
export async function createDeck(data: { title: string; description?: string }) {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) throw new Error("Unauthorized");

  const { canCreate, reason } = await canCreateDeck();
  if (!canCreate) throw new Error(reason);

  const newDeck = await db
    .insert(decksTable)
    .values({ ...data, userId })
    .returning();

  return newDeck[0];
}

// Write — update
export async function updateDeck(
  deckId: number,
  data: { title?: string; description?: string },
) {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) throw new Error("Unauthorized");

  const updatedDeck = await db
    .update(decksTable)
    .set(data)
    .where(and(eq(decksTable.id, deckId), eq(decksTable.userId, userId)))
    .returning();

  return updatedDeck[0] || null;
}

// Write — delete
export async function deleteDeck(deckId: number) {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) throw new Error("Unauthorized");

  await db
    .delete(decksTable)
    .where(and(eq(decksTable.id, deckId), eq(decksTable.userId, userId)));
}
```

### Card Queries (`src/db/queries/cards.ts`)

Cards are owned transitively through their deck. Every card function **must verify deck ownership** before operating.

```typescript
import { auth } from "@clerk/nextjs/server";
import { db } from "@/db";
import { cardsTable, decksTable } from "@/db/schema";
import { eq, and, desc } from "drizzle-orm";

// Read — all cards for a deck (verifies deck ownership first)
export async function getCardsByDeckId(deckId: number) {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) throw new Error("Unauthorized");

  const deck = await db
    .select()
    .from(decksTable)
    .where(and(eq(decksTable.id, deckId), eq(decksTable.userId, userId)))
    .limit(1);

  if (!deck.length) throw new Error("Deck not found or unauthorized");

  return await db
    .select()
    .from(cardsTable)
    .where(eq(cardsTable.deckId, deckId))
    .orderBy(desc(cardsTable.updatedAt));
}

// Write — create (verifies deck ownership)
export async function createCard(data: { deckId: number; front: string; back: string }) {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) throw new Error("Unauthorized");

  const deck = await db
    .select()
    .from(decksTable)
    .where(and(eq(decksTable.id, data.deckId), eq(decksTable.userId, userId)))
    .limit(1);

  if (!deck.length) throw new Error("Deck not found or unauthorized");

  const newCard = await db
    .insert(cardsTable)
    .values({ deckId: data.deckId, front: data.front, back: data.back })
    .returning();

  return newCard[0];
}

// Write — update (verifies deck ownership via join)
export async function updateCard(
  cardId: number,
  data: { front?: string; back?: string },
) {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) throw new Error("Unauthorized");

  const cardWithDeck = await db
    .select()
    .from(cardsTable)
    .innerJoin(decksTable, eq(cardsTable.deckId, decksTable.id))
    .where(and(eq(cardsTable.id, cardId), eq(decksTable.userId, userId)))
    .limit(1);

  if (!cardWithDeck.length) throw new Error("Card not found or unauthorized");

  const updatedCard = await db
    .update(cardsTable)
    .set({ ...data, updatedAt: new Date() })
    .where(eq(cardsTable.id, cardId))
    .returning();

  return updatedCard[0] || null;
}

// Write — delete (verifies deck ownership via join)
export async function deleteCard(cardId: number) {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) throw new Error("Unauthorized");

  const cardWithDeck = await db
    .select()
    .from(cardsTable)
    .innerJoin(decksTable, eq(cardsTable.deckId, decksTable.id))
    .where(and(eq(cardsTable.id, cardId), eq(decksTable.userId, userId)))
    .limit(1);

  if (!cardWithDeck.length) throw new Error("Card not found or unauthorized");

  await db.delete(cardsTable).where(eq(cardsTable.id, cardId));
}
```

### Re-export Index (`src/db/queries/index.ts`)

```typescript
export * from "./decks";
export * from "./cards";
```

Every new query file must be re-exported here so consumers only need `import { … } from "@/db/queries"`.

## Data Retrieval — Server Components

All reads happen in Server Components by calling query functions.

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
import { getUserDecks } from "@/db/queries";

export default async function DashboardPage() {
  const userDecks = await getUserDecks();
  return <DecksList decks={userDecks} />;
}
```

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG — direct DB access in a component
import { db } from "@/db";
import { decksTable } from "@/db/schema";

export default async function DashboardPage() {
  const decks = await db.select().from(decksTable); // violates query layer
}
```

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG — fetching in a client component
"use client";
useEffect(() => { fetch("/api/decks").then(…) }, []);
```

## Mutations — Server Actions

All writes happen in Server Actions that delegate to query functions. Server actions handle validation, call the query, then revalidate/redirect.

### Server Action Template

```typescript
"use server";

import { createCard } from "@/db/queries";
import { z } from "zod";
import { revalidatePath } from "next/cache";

// 1. Zod schema
const CreateCardSchema = z.object({
  deckId: z.number().positive(),
  front: z.string().min(1).max(1000),
  back: z.string().min(1).max(1000),
});

// 2. Derive type
type CreateCardInput = z.infer<typeof CreateCardSchema>;

// 3. Action function
export async function createCardAction(input: CreateCardInput) {
  try {
    const validatedInput = CreateCardSchema.parse(input);

    const newCard = await createCard(validatedInput);

    revalidatePath(`/decks/${validatedInput.deckId}`);

    return { success: true, card: newCard };
  } catch (error: unknown) {
    if (error instanceof z.ZodError) {
      return {
        success: false,
        error: `Validation failed: ${error.errors.map((e: z.ZodIssue) => e.message).join(", ")}`,
      };
    }
    return {
      success: false,
      error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : "An error occurred",
    };
  }
}
```

### Key rules for Server Actions

- **Always** validate with Zod before calling a query function.
- **Never** use `FormData` as the parameter type — use `z.infer<typeof Schema>`.
- **Never** import `db` or schema tables — call query functions only.
- **Never** use API route handlers (`POST`, `GET`, etc.) for mutations.
- Return `{ success: boolean; error?: string; … }` for actions consumed by client components.

## Validation

Every server action must validate input with Zod before calling any query function.

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — typed input validated with Zod
const UpdateDeckSchema = z.object({
  deckId: z.number(),
  title: z.string().min(1).max(100),
  description: z.string().max(500).optional(),
});

type UpdateDeckInput = z.infer<typeof UpdateDeckSchema>;

export async function updateDeckAction(input: UpdateDeckInput) {
  const validatedInput = UpdateDeckSchema.parse(input);
  return await updateDeck(validatedInput.deckId, {
    title: validatedInput.title,
    description: validatedInput.description,
  });
}
```

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG — untyped FormData
export async function updateDeckAction(formData: FormData) {
  const title = formData.get("title") as string;
}
```

## Error Handling

- Query functions throw on auth failure or missing resources — callers must handle these.
- Server actions catch errors and return `{ success: false, error: "…" }` for client consumption, except when using `redirect()` (which throws internally and must be re-thrown).

```typescript
export async function createDeckAction(input: CreateDeckInput) {
  try {
    const validatedInput = CreateDeckSchema.parse(input);
    const newDeck = await createDeck(validatedInput);
    redirect(`/decks/${newDeck.id}`);
  } catch (error) {
    if (error instanceof z.ZodError) {
      throw new Error(
        `Validation failed: ${error.errors.map((e) => e.message).join(", ")}`,
      );
    }
    throw error; // re-throw redirect & unexpected errors
  }
}
```

## Adding New Queries

When adding a new database operation:

1. **Create or extend** a file in `src/db/queries/` (e.g., `decks.ts`, `cards.ts`).
2. **Follow the function pattern**: `auth()` → ownership check → Drizzle query → return data.
3. **Re-export** from `src/db/queries/index.ts` if in a new file.
4. **Consume** from server components (reads) or server actions (writes) via `import { … } from "@/db/queries"`.

## Forbidden Practices

1. Importing `@/db` or `@/db/schema` outside of `src/db/queries/` files.
2. Fetching data in client components or `useEffect`.
3. Using API route handlers for mutations.
4. Skipping Zod validation in server actions.
5. Using `FormData` as a server action parameter type.
6. Duplicating auth logic — it lives in query functions.
7. Performing inline `db.select()` / `db.insert()` / `db.update()` / `db.delete()` in components or actions.
